      "message": "As far as I can see, the caller\u0027s memory is only used when `__prepare_userptr()` pins it through `get_userptr`, and `vb2_core_prepare_buf()`, `vb2_core_qbuf()` and `vb2_req_prepare()` all get there through `__buf_prepare()`. `vb2_core_dqbuf()` and `vb2_core_streamon()` only handle buffers that are already pinned, so they don\u0027t depend on the caller\u0027s page size.\n\nWould a single check at the top of `__prepare_userptr()` work instead of this helper and its five callers? It would refuse exactly where a 4KB mm would get pinned, and the REQBUFS and CREATE_BUFS checks would still give the early error.",
